{
  "id": "27020_sebiru",
  "headword": "せびる",
  "reading": "せびる",
  "romaji": "sebiru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to pester for; to cadge; to wheedle",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to pester for; to cadge; to wheedle; to beg for",
      "explanation": "To repeatedly ask someone to give you money, treats, or other things, often in an annoying or persistent way."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27020_sebiru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもがお{菓子|かし}をせびる。",
      "english": "The child pesters for sweets.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27020_sebiru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{弟|おとうと}がいつも{小遣|こづか}いをせびってくる。",
      "english": "My younger brother always pesters me for pocket money.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27020_sebiru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{友人|ゆうじん}に{飲|の}み{代|だい}をせびられて{困|こま}っている。",
      "english": "I'm troubled because a friend keeps hitting me up for drinks money.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A colloquial verb with a somewhat negative nuance. The person doing the せびる is being persistent, pushy, or shameless about asking. Common subjects are children asking parents for sweets or money, or adults shamelessly mooching off friends. Godan verb conjugating with る row.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- お{金|かね}をせびる: to pester for money\n- お{小遣|こづか}いをせびる: to beg for pocket money\n- お{菓子|かし}をせびる: to wheedle for sweets\n- おごりをせびる: to cadge a treat\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {強請|ゆす}る: to extort; to blackmail — much stronger; implies threats or coercion\n- {頼|たの}む: to ask; to request — neutral, polite request without the nuance of pestering\n- ねだる: to coax; to beg for — similar but slightly softer; often used for children begging for toys or treats",
